WEBVTT

00:00:12.887 --> 00:00:14.430
( groaning )

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:20.061
( gasping quietly )

00:00:20.103 --> 00:00:21.813
I’ve tried it on, like,
20 Oompa-Loompas,

00:00:21.896 --> 00:00:24.107
and each one ended up
as a blueberry.

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:25.733
It’s just weird.
( giggles )

00:00:25.775 --> 00:00:28.236
But I can’t have a
blueberry as a daughter.

00:00:28.319 --> 00:00:29.904
How is she supposed
to compete?

00:00:29.946 --> 00:00:31.739
You could put her
in a county fair.

00:00:31.823 --> 00:00:33.282
( giggles )

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:34.492
Oh...

00:00:34.575 --> 00:00:37.245
( oscillating tone begins )
♪ Work! ♪

00:00:37.286 --> 00:00:40.581
( mechanical rhythm plays
over funky guitar riff )

00:00:40.665 --> 00:00:44.085
♪ Work! ♪

00:00:44.127 --> 00:00:45.628
( funky riff continues )

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:47.755
♪ Yeah! ♪

00:00:47.797 --> 00:00:50.925
( horns join in )

00:00:51.009 --> 00:00:53.386
♪ Work! Yeah! ♪

00:00:53.428 --> 00:00:55.596
♪ Listen close, listen hard ♪

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:58.016
♪ The tale
of Violet Beauregarde ♪

00:00:58.099 --> 00:01:00.601
♪ This little girl,
she sits around ♪

00:01:00.643 --> 00:01:04.564
♪ Chewing, chewing, chewing
chewing, chewing, chewing ♪

00:01:04.605 --> 00:01:05.940
♪ On and on ♪

00:01:05.982 --> 00:01:07.984
♪ Chewing, chewing,
and on and on ♪

00:01:08.067 --> 00:01:10.570
♪ Chewing, chewing, and on
and on ♪

00:01:10.611 --> 00:01:13.156
♪ Chewing, chewing,
and on and on ♪

00:01:14.282 --> 00:01:15.491
♪ Yeah! ♪

00:01:18.536 --> 00:01:20.079
♪ Oompa-Loompa, Oompa-Loompa,
Oompa-Loompa, Oompa-Loompa... ♪

00:01:20.121 --> 00:01:22.540
♪ Yeah ♪

00:01:22.623 --> 00:01:24.250
♪ The girl’s a-chewing,
chew at last ♪

00:01:24.292 --> 00:01:27.170
♪ The chewing muscles
grow so fast ♪

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:29.964
♪ Violet has a giant chin ♪

00:01:30.048 --> 00:01:32.175
♪ That’s just like a violin ♪

00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:34.093
♪ Chewing, chewing, and on
and on ♪

00:01:34.135 --> 00:01:36.554
♪ Chewing, chewing
and on and on ♪

00:01:36.637 --> 00:01:37.555
Whoa... oh... oh...!

00:01:37.638 --> 00:01:39.348
♪ Chewing, chewing on and on ♪

00:01:39.432 --> 00:01:41.601
♪ Oompa-Loompa, Oompa-Loompa
Oompa-Loompa, Oompa-Loompa ♪

00:01:41.642 --> 00:01:43.478
♪ Oompa-Loompa, Oompa-Loompa,
Oompa-Loompa... ♪

00:01:43.519 --> 00:01:46.147
♪ For years and years,
she chews away ♪

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:47.690
♪ Her jaws get stronger
every day ♪

00:01:47.774 --> 00:01:48.775
( screaming )

00:01:48.816 --> 00:01:50.902
♪ And with one great
tremendous chew ♪

00:01:50.985 --> 00:01:53.362
♪ And out the poor girl’s
tongue had chewed ♪

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:55.573
♪ And that is why
we try so hard ♪

00:01:55.656 --> 00:01:57.158
♪ To save Miss Violet
Beauregarde ♪

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:58.367
( groaning )

00:01:58.451 --> 00:02:00.286
♪ Chewing, chewing, and on
and on ♪

00:02:00.328 --> 00:02:02.205
♪ Chewing, chewing,
and on and on ♪

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:03.581
♪ Chewing and chewing and
chewing ♪

00:02:03.664 --> 00:02:05.249
♪ And chewing,
chewing, chewing ♪

00:02:05.333 --> 00:02:07.168
VIOLET:
Help! Please Help!

00:02:07.251 --> 00:02:08.377
♪ On and on ♪

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:10.505
♪ Chewing, chewing and on
and on ♪

00:02:10.546 --> 00:02:13.007
♪ Chewing, chewing
and on and on... ♪

00:02:13.049 --> 00:02:16.928
VIOLET:
Mr. Wonka!

00:02:17.011 --> 00:02:21.224
( song fades out )

00:02:21.307 --> 00:02:22.517
I want you to

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:24.519
roll Miss Beauregarde
into the boat and

00:02:24.602 --> 00:02:27.355
take her along to the
juicing room at once.

00:02:27.438 --> 00:02:28.940
Okay?

00:02:29.023 --> 00:02:30.358
The juicing room?

00:02:30.441 --> 00:02:31.859
What are they gonna do
to her there?

00:02:31.943 --> 00:02:34.028
Uh, they’re gonna squeeze her

00:02:34.070 --> 00:02:36.280
like a little pimple.

00:02:36.364 --> 00:02:37.949
We got to
squeeze all that

00:02:38.032 --> 00:02:40.201
juice out of her immediately.

00:02:40.243 --> 00:02:41.577
( quiet sob )

00:02:41.661 --> 00:02:43.955
VIOLET:
Mother,

00:02:44.038 --> 00:02:46.290
help me, please!

00:02:47.917 --> 00:02:49.877
( grunting )

00:02:51.963 --> 00:02:54.006
Come on.

00:02:54.048 --> 00:02:55.341
Let’s boogie.

00:02:55.383 --> 00:02:56.884
WONKA:
Without the boat,

00:02:56.968 --> 00:02:59.095
we’ll have to move double-time,
just to keep on schedule.

00:02:59.178 --> 00:03:00.179
There’s far too much to see.

00:03:00.221 --> 00:03:01.639
Mr. Wonka?
Yeah.

00:03:01.722 --> 00:03:03.641
Why did you decide
to let people in?

00:03:03.724 --> 00:03:05.935
Oh, so they could see
the factory, of course.

00:03:06.018 --> 00:03:07.895
But why now, and
why only five?

00:03:07.979 --> 00:03:09.021
MIKE:
What’s the special

00:03:09.063 --> 00:03:10.273
prize, and who gets it?

00:03:10.356 --> 00:03:12.859
The best kind
of prize is a surprise.

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:14.235
( laughs )

00:03:14.318 --> 00:03:16.445
Will Violet always be
a blueberry?

00:03:16.529 --> 00:03:18.656
No. Maybe.
I don’t know.

00:03:18.739 --> 00:03:20.867
But that’s what you get
from chewing gum all day.

00:03:20.908 --> 00:03:22.118
It’s just disgusting.

00:03:22.201 --> 00:03:24.203
If you hate gum so much,
why do you make it?

00:03:24.245 --> 00:03:25.788
Once again,
you really shouldn’t mumble,

00:03:25.872 --> 00:03:27.623
’cause it’s kind of starting
to bum me out.

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:30.209
Can you remember the first candy
you ever ate?

00:03:34.088 --> 00:03:35.131
No.

00:03:35.214 --> 00:03:36.465
NARRATOR:
In fact, Willy Wonka

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:40.928
did remember the first candy
he ever ate.

00:03:50.271 --> 00:03:52.607
♪ ♪

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:04.452
♪ ♪

00:04:13.294 --> 00:04:16.964
♪ ♪

00:04:25.181 --> 00:04:27.516
♪ ♪

00:04:37.193 --> 00:04:39.362
♪ ♪

00:04:40.988 --> 00:04:42.448
I’m sorry.

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:44.700
I was having a flashback.

00:04:45.743 --> 00:04:47.578
I see.

00:04:47.662 --> 00:04:49.872
These flashbacks happen often?

00:04:49.956 --> 00:04:51.832
Increasingly.

00:04:51.916 --> 00:04:53.000
Today.

00:04:53.042 --> 00:04:54.752
( giggles )

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:03.010
Ah, this is a room
I know all about,

00:05:03.094 --> 00:05:04.220
for you see,
Mr. Wonka,

00:05:04.303 --> 00:05:06.138
I myself am in
the nut business.

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:08.015
Are you using
the Havimax 4000

00:05:08.099 --> 00:05:10.059
to do your sorting?

00:05:10.142 --> 00:05:11.310
No.

00:05:11.352 --> 00:05:13.562
( laughs )
You’re really weird.

00:05:18.526 --> 00:05:21.862
( light clattering,
high-pitched chattering )

00:05:30.371 --> 00:05:33.416
( chattering continues )

00:05:34.292 --> 00:05:35.251
Squirrels!

00:05:35.334 --> 00:05:36.335
WONKA:
Yeah!

00:05:36.377 --> 00:05:37.503
Squirrels.

00:05:37.545 --> 00:05:39.130
These squirrels
are specially trained

00:05:39.213 --> 00:05:40.881
to get the nuts
out of shells.

00:05:40.923 --> 00:05:42.925
( chattering )

00:05:43.009 --> 00:05:44.719
( shells cracking )

00:05:50.558 --> 00:05:52.435
( clattering )

00:05:56.522 --> 00:05:57.523
Why use squirrels?

00:05:57.565 --> 00:05:59.358
Why not use Oompa-Loompas?

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:01.360
Because only squirrels
can get

00:06:01.402 --> 00:06:03.487
the whole walnut out
almost every single time.

00:06:05.031 --> 00:06:07.241
You see how they tap each one
with their little knuckles,

00:06:07.325 --> 00:06:08.367
to make sure it’s not bad?

00:06:08.409 --> 00:06:09.660
Oh, look, look!

00:06:11.495 --> 00:06:13.748
I think that one’s got
a bad nut.

00:06:15.207 --> 00:06:18.419
Daddy, I want a squirrel.
Get me one of those squirrels.

00:06:18.461 --> 00:06:19.795
I want one.

00:06:19.879 --> 00:06:22.298
Veruca, dear, you have
many marvelous pets.

00:06:22.381 --> 00:06:24.258
All I’ve got at home

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:26.344
is one pony and two dogs
and four cats

00:06:26.427 --> 00:06:28.220
and six bunny rabbits
and two parakeets

00:06:28.262 --> 00:06:29.555
and three canaries
and a green parrot

00:06:29.597 --> 00:06:31.390
and a turtle and a
silly old hamster!

00:06:31.432 --> 00:06:33.809
I want a squirrel!

00:06:33.893 --> 00:06:36.437
All right, pet.
Daddy’ll get you a squirrel,

00:06:36.479 --> 00:06:37.855
just as soon as
he possibly can.

00:06:37.938 --> 00:06:40.274
VERUCA:
But I don’t want
any old squirrel.

00:06:40.358 --> 00:06:42.485
I want a trained squirrel.

00:06:43.444 --> 00:06:44.737
Very well.

00:06:44.779 --> 00:06:45.780
Mr. Wonka?

00:06:45.821 --> 00:06:47.615
How much do you
want for one

00:06:47.698 --> 00:06:49.575
of these squirrels?
Name your price.

00:06:51.285 --> 00:06:52.953
Uh, they’re not for sale.

00:06:52.995 --> 00:06:54.622
She can’t have one.

00:06:58.834 --> 00:07:00.669
Daddy!

00:07:02.088 --> 00:07:03.798
( upper-crust accent ):
I’m sorry, darling.

00:07:03.881 --> 00:07:06.675
Mr. Wonka is being
unreasonable.

00:07:08.386 --> 00:07:12.765
If you won’t get me a squirrel,
I’ll get one myself.

